### Auth handshake walkthrough — authentication-service
# Family SSO: passwordless magic-link -> Postgres cookie session ->
# short-lived PASETO v4.public cross-service token -> bearer call on a peer.
# See agents/share/authentication-sessions.md §5 for the full design, and
# agents/share/authorization-attributes.md for the `attrs` claim / ABAC.
#
# Response envelope here is BARE loco JSON (no {"success":...} wrapper) —
# see src/controllers/auth.rs. Run these top to bottom: each later request
# needs a cookie or token value a prior one produced.
#
# `AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRE_AUTH`-style gating does not apply to this crate
# itself (it is the issuer); the peer call at the bottom demonstrates a
# service that DOES gate on `<ENTITY>_REQUIRE_AUTH`, which is off by
# default in examples/compose/full-family.yml (agents/share/security.md §4)
# — so step 6 succeeds with or without a real bearer token against the
# stock compose file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8091
@personBaseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@email = demo@example.com


### 1. Sign up (or re-request a magic link for an existing account).
# Always returns 200 {} regardless of whether the email is new, rate
# limited, or rejected — this is a deliberate anti-enumeration contract
# (src/controllers/auth.rs). It does NOT return the token in the body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "name": "Demo User"
}


### 2. Retrieve the magic-link token — dev mode, no real mailbox.
# SMTP is disabled in config/development.yaml; the mail send is
# best-effort and fails silently. The AUTHORITATIVE way to get the token
# locally is the tracing console log line:
#
#   magic link issued (dev: open the link, or GET /api/auth/magic-link/{token})
#
# Read it with:
#   podman compose -f examples/compose/full-family.yml logs authentication-service \
#     | grep 'magic link issued' | tail -1
#
# Copy the token that appears after `?token=` (or the bare `magic_link`
# field, depending on log formatter) into @magicLinkToken below.
@magicLinkToken = REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN_FROM_LOG


### 3. Verify the magic link — consumes the token, establishes the session.
# GET, not POST: the token rides in the path, no body. On success:
#  - body is LoginResponse: {"token","pid","name","email","is_verified"}
#    (the "token" field here is a PASETO v4.public string, despite the
#    doc-comment in the crate calling it an "access token" — that comment
#    is stale, see agents/share/authentication-sessions.md).
#  - TWO Set-Cookie headers: __Host-mxi_session (HttpOnly) and
#    __Host-mxi_csrf (readable — the BFF needs to read it to echo it back).
# A client without automatic cookie-jar support (plain curl, or a REST
# client with cookies disabled) must copy both values by hand into
# @sessionCookie / @csrfToken below.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/magic-link/{{magicLinkToken}}

@sessionCookie = REPLACE_WITH_Host-mxi_session_COOKIE_VALUE
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_Host-mxi_csrf_COOKIE_VALUE


### 4. Exchange the session for a short-lived PASETO v4.public token.
# Requires the session cookie AND the CSRF header (constant-time compared
# against the hashed cookie value server-side, src/csrf.rs). No body.
# Response: bare {"token": "v4.public...."} — note this is NOT the same
# shape as step 3's LoginResponse.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Cookie: __Host-mxi_session={{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}

@bearerToken = REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_4_RESPONSE


### 5. Introspect the current session with the freshly-minted bearer token.
# GET /api/auth/me is gated on Authorization: Bearer, not the cookie —
# it independently re-checks the session (by the token's `sid` claim) is
# still active and slides the idle TTL.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}


### 6. Fetch the published Ed25519 key set every peer verifies against.
# No auth required — this is the public discovery endpoint
# (agents/share/authentication-sessions.md §5, the JWKS analogue).
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/paseto-keys


### 7a. Use the bearer token on an ordinary PEER endpoint (person-service).
# With PERSON_REQUIRE_AUTH off (the compose default, curl-verified) this
# succeeds with or without the header — the blanket guard is a no-op.
# Accepts-version demonstrates the header-based versioning scheme
# (agents/share/api-versioning.md).
GET {{personBaseUrl}}/api/persons/search?q=&limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}
Accepts-version: 1.0


### 7b. Use the bearer token on the peer's OWN introspection endpoint.
# UNLIKE ordinary endpoints, /api/whoami always demands a valid bearer —
# curl-verified: it 401s "missing authorization header" with none, REGARDLESS
# of PERSON_REQUIRE_AUTH. With this handshake's real token it still 401s,
# with "no verification key for kid ..." — examples/compose/full-family.yml
# does not wire PERSON_PASETO_KEYS_URL at authentication-service, so
# person-service's verifier holds zero keys. This is a genuine gap in the
# demo compose (not a doc error): to make this call succeed, set
# PERSON_PASETO_KEYS_URL=http://authentication-service:5150/.well-known/paseto-keys
# on person-service and restart it.
GET {{personBaseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}


### 8. Sign out — clears both cookies server-side, revokes the session.
# Subsequent calls to step 4 (POST /api/auth/token) with the same session
# cookie will now 401; a bearer token already minted keeps working until
# it naturally expires (~5 min) — see authentication-sessions.md §3 on
# why revocation is immediate for new tokens but not retroactive.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signout
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}


### 9. (Admin only) List a user's ABAC attributes.
# Requires a bearer token whose `attrs.access` includes "admin" — the
# bootstrap admin is assigned out-of-band via the `user_attributes` CLI
# task (src/tasks/attributes.rs), not over HTTP. Included here to show
# the shape; expect 403 unless you've bootstrapped an admin locally.
# @pid is the "pid" field from step 3's LoginResponse.
@pid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_STEP_3

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users/{{pid}}/attributes
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}


### 10. (Admin only) Replace a user's ABAC attributes.
# Full replacement, not a merge. Keys/values are short lowercase tokens;
# "sub"/"email"/"entity" are reserved. On success, every existing session
# for this user is revoked (so a stale token can't outlive its old
# attributes) and an `attributes_assigned` audit row is written.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users/{{pid}}/attributes
Authorization: Bearer {{bearerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attributes": {
    "access": ["write"],
    "dept": ["cardiology"]
  }
}
